<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav copper ore output falls in Sept.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav copper ore output falls in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV NON-FERROUS ORES    Sept 96    Aug 96	Sept 95</p>
<p> copper (thousand tonnes)	1,678	1,807	 1,608</p>
<p> lead-zinc				72	   81	    56</p>
<p> bauxite				  20	   60	    16</p>
<p>NON-FERROUS METAL PRODUCTION</p>
<p> electrolytic copper (tonnes) 10,025     11,368	 6,350</p>
<p> refined lead			1,165	3,440	 2,334</p>
<p> zinc				  2,298	3,205	 2,262</p>
<p> aluminium ingots		  3,364	3,769	 2,273</p>
<p> refined silver (kg)	     2,712	7,083	 6,070</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
</text>
